294
00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:34.460
He does?
真的吗？

295
00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:35.140
Yes.
是的。

296
00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:36.340
What does he do in that episode?
他在那一集里做了什么？

297
00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:38.940
He was actually there to interview for a job.
他其实是去面试工作的。

298
00:13:38.940 --> 00:13:40.040
Oh, I remember that.
哦，我想起来了。

299
00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:46.100
Oh, Dwight brings in a bunch of his old friends and weirdos to interview.
哦，Dwight带了一堆他的老朋友和怪人来面试。

300
00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:47.120
And, like, family members.
还有，比如，家庭成员。

301
00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:47.600
Yes.
是的。

302
00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:52.660
Lance emailed me a great behind-the-scenes photo of him and the other people interviewing
兰斯给我发了一张很棒的幕后照片，是他和其他人在会议室面试工作时的合影。

303
00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:54.040
for jobs in the conference room.
会议室。

304
00:13:54.040 --> 00:14:00.540
And he has his karate outfit on over a business suit.
他穿着空手道服，里面还套着西装。

305
00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:02.120
So his tie is, like, poking out.
所以他的领带就那样露在外面。

306
00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:03.320
It's, like, so odd.
看起来真是太奇怪了。

307
00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:06.660
But, yeah, he was on season one and then on season nine.
不过，没错，他参加了第一季和第九季的拍摄。

308
00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:10.600
So he sort of had this great perspective of being on the bookends of the show.
所以他以一种独特的视角，见证了这部剧的始末。

309
00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.460
What a very, very cool thing.
这真是太酷了。

310
00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:12.880
Yeah.
没错。

311
00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:17.700
Thank you so much, Lance, for taking time out of your schedule in Atlanta to chat me up.
非常感谢兰斯，在亚特兰大的百忙之中抽出时间和我聊天。

312
00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:20.200
And we're going to call you again come Junior Salesman.
等拍到“初级销售员”那一集时，我们还会再联系你。

313
00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:21.440
Yeah, I love it.
好啊，我很乐意。

314
00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:24.900
All right, let's take a break and we'll be back to break down the fight.
好了，我们先休息一下，回来后再详细分析那场打斗。

315
00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:31.310
We are back.
我们回来了。

316
00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:31.850
Hello.
大家好。

317
00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:35.110
This episode begins with a prank.
这一集以一个恶作剧开始。

318
00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:38.770
Jim pranks Dwight by putting his desk in the bathroom.
吉姆把德怀特的办公桌搬进了洗手间，以此捉弄他。

319
00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:40.570
Oh, poor Dwight.
噢，可怜的德怀特。

320
00:14:40.570 --> 00:14:41.410
This was a good one.
这个恶作剧很棒。

321
00:14:41.570 --> 00:14:42.590
This was a good prank.
这真是一个精彩的恶作剧。

322
00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:43.630
I like this one.
我很喜欢这个。

323
00:14:43.850 --> 00:14:47.430
You have to look for Kevin in the background at the end when he leaves one of the stalls.
你们一定要留意结尾处凯文从隔间出来时的背景。

324
00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:49.730
He has a lit candle and a newspaper.
他手里拿着一支点燃的蜡烛和一份报纸。

325
00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:55.470
And for all of you office geeks, this was the moment that led to Kevin's line in Office
对于所有《办公室》的铁粉来说，正是这一幕引出了后来在“办公室奥运会”里，

326
00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:58.870
Olympics about the bathroom candle smelling like cookies.
凯文说洗手间的蜡烛闻起来像饼干的台词。

327
00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:05.550
Also, remember that in the Dundies, he did win the Don't Go In There After Me award.
另外，别忘了在“邓迪奖”颁奖礼上，他确实赢得了“千万别在我之后进去”奖。

328
00:15:05.810 --> 00:15:06.130
Yes.
没错。

329
00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:07.650
And I think we see why.
我想我们现在明白原因了。

330
00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:12.590
Also, though, guys, who is lighting candles inside the stall?
不过话说回来，伙计们，到底是谁在隔间里点蜡烛啊？

331
00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:16.230
Like, he doesn't come out and light the candle.
他不是出来之后才点的蜡烛。

332
00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:20.310
He exits the stall holding a candle, a lit candle.
他是拿着一支点燃的蜡烛从隔间里走出来的。

333
00:15:20.570 --> 00:15:20.950
Yes.
没错。

334
00:15:21.130 --> 00:15:22.790
And that candle really did smell like cookies.
那支蜡烛闻起来确实像饼干。

335
00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:23.730
I want to say that.
我得提一下这一点。

336
00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:28.210
Did you notice that there is another door by the urinal?
你们注意到小便池旁边还有另一扇门吗？

337
00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:30.050
Angela, where does it go?
安吉拉，那扇门通向哪里？

338
00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:30.930
We don't know.
我们不知道。

339
00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:32.430
I like to think maybe.
我倾向于认为也许……

340
00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:32.990
What is that door?
那扇门是什么？

341
00:15:33.150 --> 00:15:34.390
Is it a utility closet?
是个杂物间吗？

342
00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:35.130
That's what I think.
我也是这么想的。

343
00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:37.530
I think there's like a mop in there or something.
我觉得里面可能放着拖把之类的东西。

344
00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:38.490
That's my guess.
我猜是这样。

345
00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:39.070
Yeah.
没错。

346
00:15:39.390 --> 00:15:40.910
Those bathrooms did not work.
那些洗手间其实根本不能用。

347
00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:41.290
Nope.
没错。

348
00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:42.390
It was very deceiving.
太有欺骗性了。

349
00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:46.850
We would have people come visit us on the set, like guests, family members, and they
当时会有客人、家属之类的来片场探班，他们

350
00:15:46.850 --> 00:15:50.690
would go in there thinking that they were real bathrooms and they weren't.
会以为那是真正的洗手间就走进去，但其实并不是。

351
00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:51.090
No.
不。

352
00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:53.790
In the next scene, Dwight calls his sensei.
下一场戏里，德怀特给他的师傅打了电话。

353
00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:56.070
Jim asks if he's talking to his mother.
吉姆问他是不是在跟他妈妈说话。

354
00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:57.030
I love that.
我喜欢那个。

355
00:15:57.030 --> 00:15:58.650
I think John is really good in that scene.
我觉得约翰在那场戏里演得真好。

356
00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:05.930
And then there is his whole talking head about being a sensei, an assistant to the sensei.
还有他关于自己是师傅、师傅助手的整段采访。

357
00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:06.770
What is it?
那是什么？

358
00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:11.710
So yeah, Dwight says he's the senpai, which is basically like the assistant to the sensei.
所以，是的，德怀特说他是“先辈”，基本上就是师傅的助手。

359
00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:12.130
Yeah.
没错。

360
00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:12.870
Although-
虽然——

361
00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:13.810
Not assistant sensei.
不是助理师傅。

362
00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:14.190
Right.
对。

363
00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:16.270
But also, actually, it's not him.
但其实，那个人不是他。

364
00:16:16.630 --> 00:16:17.670
It's like the girl.
是那个女孩。

365
00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:18.110
Remember?
还记得吗？

366
00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:21.810
Because later in the episode, Sensei Ira is like, there's my senpai.
因为在这一集的后面，艾拉师傅说：“那是我的先辈。”

367
00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:23.890
So we learn that it's actually not Dwight.
所以我们才知道那其实不是德怀特。

368
00:16:24.030 --> 00:16:24.570
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

369
00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:25.570
I missed that.
我没注意到。

370
00:16:25.890 --> 00:16:26.130
Yeah.
是啊。

371
00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:27.930
The girl that walks through the scene.
那个走过镜头前的女孩。

372
00:16:28.030 --> 00:16:28.310
Yeah.
对。

373
00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:29.530
Is actually the senpai.
才是真正的先辈。

374
00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:31.830
Oh, I totally missed that.
噢，我完全没注意到。

375
00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:32.550
All right.
好吧。

376
00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:34.910
So next, we have Pam's talking head.
接下来是帕姆的采访。

377
00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:46.490
And this is when we find out that today is the day that Michael has to sign time cards, purchase order approvals, and expense reports that they're all due at the end of the day.
我们在这儿得知，今天迈克尔必须签署考勤卡、采购订单审批和费用报告，这些都必须在今天下班前完成。

378
00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:51.390
And this happens a couple times a year, and he always procrastinates wildly on these days.
这种情况一年会发生几次，而他在这些日子里总是会疯狂拖延。

379
00:16:52.010 --> 00:16:57.470
As a former secretary, I really relate to the dynamic between Pam and Michael in this episode.
作为一名前秘书，我真的对这一集里帕姆和迈克尔之间的互动感同身受。

380
00:16:57.630 --> 00:17:00.190
Because during one of my early secretarial jobs,
因为在我早期的秘书工作中，

381
00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:12.330
I had a boss that would take so long to do his end of the month report that I would have to drive to the airport because the FedEx at the airport had the latest drop time.
我有个老板做月度报告总是拖很久，以至于我不得不开车去机场，因为机场的联邦快递投递截止时间最晚。

382
00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:20.210
I'm saying LAX airport, which anyone who lives in Los Angeles, if I drive to LAX now, it's about a two-hour drive.
我说的是洛杉矶国际机场，任何住在洛杉矶的人都知道，如果我现在开车去那里，大概要花两个小时。

383
00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:24.750
So I would have to drive to the airport for like the 7 p.m.
所以我得开车去机场赶晚上7点的投递。

384
00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:27.210
It might have even been 9 p.m.
甚至可能是晚上9点的。

385
00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:28.050
FedEx drop.
联邦快递投递。

386
00:17:28.050 --> 00:17:29.210
Also, there's nowhere to park.
而且，那里根本没地方停车。

387
00:17:29.410 --> 00:17:29.990
Nowhere to park.
根本没地方停车。

388
00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:31.930
And people are blowing whistles at you.
人们还一直对你吹哨子。

389
00:17:31.930 --> 00:17:32.290
Yes.
没错。

390
00:17:32.470 --> 00:17:33.590
Like, move out of the way.
就像在说，快让开。

391
00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:34.450
It's like chaos.
简直是一团糟。

392
00:17:34.730 --> 00:17:36.950
I do love that Pam calls it the perfect storm.
我确实很喜欢帕姆把它称为“完美风暴”。

393
00:17:37.270 --> 00:17:38.150
I do too.
我也喜欢。

394
00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:41.290
Also, though, Michael isn't having even to do any work.
不过话说回来，迈克尔甚至都不用做什么工作。

395
00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:42.990
It's not like he's having to put together a report.
又不是让他去写报告。

396
00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:44.850
All he has to do is sign them.
他只需要签个字就行了。

397
00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:45.830
It's so basic.
这太基础了。

398
00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:46.130
That's right.
没错。

399
00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:47.610
It's just his signature.
只需要他的签名而已。

400
00:17:47.930 --> 00:17:49.810
It could take him like 20 minutes.
这顶多花他20分钟。

401
00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:50.230
Yeah.
是啊。

402
00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:51.550
And he'd be done.
然后他就搞定了。

403
00:17:51.770 --> 00:18:00.990
This is why I would get so mad at my boss who couldn't manage to get his report done because I would think to myself, it's not new information.
这就是为什么我会对我老板那么生气，他总是没法按时完成报告，因为我心想，这又不是什么新信息。

404
00:18:01.190 --> 00:18:05.570
It's a boilerplate report that you have to do every month.
这只是每个月都要做的例行报告。

405
00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:09.070
It wasn't a special project that sneaked up on us.
又不是什么突然冒出来的特殊项目。

406
00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:09.710
Yeah.
没错。

407
00:18:09.910 --> 00:18:10.950
Time management, dude.
时间管理啊，老兄。

408
00:18:10.950 --> 00:18:14.690
You can see I'm still, I'm still a little angry about it.
你看我到现在，还是有点生气。

409
00:18:14.730 --> 00:18:18.730
Well, if I had to drive to the airport to mail something, I'd be ticked off for a long time.
好吧，如果我得开车去机场寄东西，我也会气很久的。

410
00:18:18.890 --> 00:18:19.270
All right.
好吧。

411
00:18:19.430 --> 00:18:25.210
So next up in Michael's attempt to procrastinate, he tells Ryan to update the emergency contacts.
接下来是迈克尔为了拖延时间，让瑞安去更新紧急联系人名单。

412
00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:31.450
So I enter that scene where Michael is telling Ryan to do the emergency contact liSt.
所以我进入了那个场景，迈克尔正让瑞安去弄紧急联系人名单。

413
00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:37.270
I was so concentrated on not laughing at Steve who was being so funny in that scene.
我当时全神贯注地忍着不笑，因为史蒂夫在那场戏里实在太搞笑了。

414
00:18:37.270 --> 00:18:46.650
It took everything I had that when BJ would look at me and say the line, updating emergency contacts, I lost it.
我费了九牛二虎之力，但当BJ看着我说出那句台词“更新紧急联系人”时，我还是破功了。

415
00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:50.990
But I started, it became, you know, in the scenes where you can't stop laughing and you have a trigger?
但我开始……你知道，在那些你忍不住笑场的戏里，总有个触发点，对吧？

416
00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:51.530
Yeah.
是啊。

417
00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:58.490
It was BJ turning to me and very sadly saying, updating emergency contacts.
就是BJ转过头来，非常悲伤地对我说：“更新紧急联系人”。

418
00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:04.230
I think I only got through one scene and I did it by not looking at BJ in the eye.
我想我只拍过一次就过了，还是因为我没敢直视BJ的眼睛。

419
00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:05.570
Like I stared at his forehead.
我就盯着他的额头看。

420
00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:09.410
I spent nine years looking at Steve Carell's forehead.
我盯着史蒂夫·卡瑞尔的额头看了九年。

421
00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:14.970
Because if I made eye contact with Steve, I used to say he would just like suck out your soul.
因为如果我和史蒂夫有眼神交流，我常说他会把你的灵魂吸走。

422
00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:17.610
You made eye contact with him through comedy.
你通过喜剧和他进行了眼神交流。

423
00:19:17.610 --> 00:19:20.410
I could not lock eyes with him or I would start laughing.
我不能和他对视，否则我就会笑场。

424
00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:21.290
So I would.
所以我只能……

425
00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:22.210
I would look at his forehead.
我只能盯着他的额头看。

426
00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:24.190
Every conference room scene.
每一场会议室的戏都是这样。

427
00:19:24.310 --> 00:19:26.050
I would have to do that or look at someone's ear.
我必须这样做，或者盯着别人的耳朵看。

428
00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:26.770
Yes.
没错。

429
00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:27.810
Or their eyebrows.
或者盯着他们的眉毛。

430
00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:28.750
Yeah, their neck.
是啊，还有脖子。

431
00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:29.190
Yeah.
没错。

432
00:19:29.510 --> 00:19:30.830
Just not in the eyes.
就是不能看眼睛。

433
00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:32.270
Not in the eyes.
不能看眼睛。

434
00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:34.870
Well, I thought that was a major Pam Sass moment.
我觉得那是帕姆非常毒舌的一个瞬间。

435
00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:37.950
I think you have two really good Pam Sass moments in this episode.
我觉得这一集里你有两个非常棒的帕姆毒舌瞬间。

436
00:19:38.090 --> 00:19:40.410
And one of them is where you just walk out while he's talking.
其中一个就是在他说话的时候你直接走开了。

437
00:19:40.710 --> 00:19:42.490
And he's like, oh, she just left it.
然后他说，哦，她就这么走了。

438
00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:43.850
When he finished talking.
在他还没说完的时候。

439
00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:49.390
I was really channeling my real life experience working for that crazy guy.
我当时真的把为那个疯子工作的真实生活经验带入进去了。

440
00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:53.350
Michael gets Ryan's phone number in this episode.
迈克尔在这一集里拿到了瑞安的电话号码。

441
00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:54.090
Oh, man.
天呐。

442
00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:54.690
He's so delighted.
他高兴坏了。

443
00:19:54.890 --> 00:19:56.350
He keeps calling him and doing voices.
他不停地给他打电话，还变换着嗓音。

444
00:19:56.610 --> 00:19:58.010
And Angela, flip phone.
还有安吉拉的翻盖手机。

445
00:19:58.310 --> 00:19:59.190
Flip phone.
翻盖手机。

446
00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:02.250
Outdated phone is very featured in this episode.
过时的手机在这一集里戏份很重。

447
00:20:02.570 --> 00:20:07.630
As is my favorite thing is when Steve as Michael Scott cracks himself up.
我最喜欢的一点就是史蒂夫饰演的迈克尔·斯科特自己把自己逗乐的时候。

448
00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:09.270
It's like one of my favorite things.
那是我最喜欢的事情之一。

449
00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:10.050
Yes.
没错。

450
