00:32:26.960 --> 00:32:27.260
Yes.
知道。

777
00:32:27.740 --> 00:32:28.740
Because Steve would do this thing.
因为史蒂夫会做那个动作。

778
00:32:28.880 --> 00:32:32.260
So, the waiter, he's a waiter, but food makes him nauseous.
那个服务员，他是个服务员，但食物会让他反胃。

779
00:32:32.320 --> 00:32:35.560
So, he would walk up to a table and have to give the specials of the day.
所以他走到桌边报今日特供的时候。

780
00:32:35.560 --> 00:32:38.040
So, he'd be like, so ask me, Jenna, what are the specials of the day?
他会说，来，珍娜，问我今日特供是什么？

781
00:32:38.140 --> 00:32:39.120
What are the specials of the day?
今日特供是什么？

782
00:32:39.880 --> 00:32:42.680
Well, we have broccoli.
嗯，我们有西兰花。

783
00:32:44.880 --> 00:32:49.060
He would start to puke as he listed off the specials.
他在报菜名的时候就开始干呕。

784
00:32:49.060 --> 00:32:49.320
Yes.
没错。

785
00:32:49.400 --> 00:32:54.720
He'd be like, we have a delicious chicken with a cream sauce.
他会说，我们有美味的奶油酱鸡肉。

786
00:32:56.140 --> 00:32:57.360
Sorry, cream sauce.
抱歉，奶油酱。

787
00:32:57.620 --> 00:32:59.160
It was so hilarious.
太搞笑了。

788
00:32:59.800 --> 00:33:00.420
It's so good.
真的太棒了。

789
00:33:00.480 --> 00:33:01.400
We are not doing it justice.
我们描述得一点都不传神。

790
00:33:01.400 --> 00:33:03.120
We are not doing justice to it at all.
我们完全没能还原出那种效果。

791
00:33:03.120 --> 00:33:03.540
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

792
00:33:03.620 --> 00:33:05.660
If Steve ever comes on our podcaSt.
如果史蒂夫能来我们的播客。

793
00:33:05.960 --> 00:33:06.860
Do you think he would do that?
你觉得他会表演吗？

794
00:33:07.300 --> 00:33:07.700
Yes.
会。

795
00:33:07.880 --> 00:33:08.520
Oh, I need him.
噢，我太需要他了。

796
00:33:08.520 --> 00:33:09.420
I need him to do it.
我一定要让他表演一下。

797
00:33:09.460 --> 00:33:12.000
Oh, Steve, come on and do Nauseous Waiter for us.
噢，史蒂夫，快来给我们表演一下“反胃的服务员”吧。

798
00:33:12.140 --> 00:33:12.190
Yes.
没错。

799
00:33:12.300 --> 00:33:14.420
We would make him do that.
我们一定会逼他表演的。

800
00:33:14.540 --> 00:33:15.100
We loved that.
我们太爱那个桥段了。

801
00:33:15.580 --> 00:33:17.000
Angela, I think we should go to a break.
安吉拉，我觉得我们该休息一下了。

802
00:33:17.200 --> 00:33:17.940
I think we should.
我也觉得该休息了。

803
00:33:18.060 --> 00:33:20.220
I would like to go eat some chips.
我想去吃点薯片。

804
00:33:20.360 --> 00:33:24.860
Maybe some sour cream and onion chips from the basket.
也许是篮子里的酸奶油洋葱味薯片。

805
00:33:25.020 --> 00:33:27.880
Well, clearly, you just want to be the gift that keeps on giving in here.
好吧，显然你就是想在这里源源不断地给大家带来惊喜。

806
00:33:29.120 --> 00:33:29.520
Yes.
没错。

807
00:33:29.720 --> 00:33:29.940
All right.
好的。

808
00:33:29.980 --> 00:33:30.620
We'll see you in a second.
我们稍后回来。

809
00:33:35.500 --> 00:33:36.420
We're back from break.
我们休息回来了。

810
00:33:36.580 --> 00:33:36.960
Angela.
安吉拉。

811
00:33:37.240 --> 00:33:37.640
Yes.
怎么了？

812
00:33:37.900 --> 00:33:39.280
I have a time code.
我有个时间码。

813
00:33:39.640 --> 00:33:40.040
What?
什么？

814
00:33:40.400 --> 00:33:40.680
Yeah.
对。

815
00:33:41.080 --> 00:33:43.300
I actually, I have three time codes.
其实，我有三个时间码。

816
00:33:43.500 --> 00:33:44.900
Jenna, I'm so proud of you.
珍娜，我真为你感到骄傲。

817
00:33:45.040 --> 00:33:45.320
Thank you.
谢谢。

818
00:33:45.460 --> 00:33:51.160
I almost, I almost wrote them on note cards and brought in three note cards, but I didn't
我差点，我差点把它们写在卡片上带过来，但我不想

819
00:33:51.160 --> 00:33:53.880
want to infringe on your note card thing.
侵犯你的卡片专利。

820
00:33:54.480 --> 00:33:56.420
First of all, I don't own note cards.
首先，我并没有什么卡片专利。

821
00:33:56.580 --> 00:33:57.340
I encourage you.
我很鼓励你这么做。

822
00:33:57.460 --> 00:33:57.960
I love it.
我喜欢这样。

823
00:33:58.160 --> 00:33:58.540
Use it.
尽管用吧。

824
00:33:58.920 --> 00:34:00.480
I mean, Jenna, you don't own a liSt.
我是说，珍娜，你根本就没有列清单的习惯。

825
00:34:00.700 --> 00:34:01.700
I hate to break it to you.
很抱歉要打破你的幻想。

826
00:34:01.780 --> 00:34:03.200
I might come in someday with a liSt.
也许哪天我会带着清单来。

827
00:34:03.600 --> 00:34:04.920
I think that's fantastic.
我觉得那太棒了。

828
00:34:04.920 --> 00:34:06.180
What is your time code?
你的时间码是多少？

829
00:34:06.240 --> 00:34:07.600
Well, I was very excited.
嗯，我当时非常兴奋。

830
00:34:07.920 --> 00:34:15.400
It's 11 minutes, 50 seconds, and it is the scene where Pam and Jim are walking to the
是11分50秒，那是帕姆和吉姆走向

831
00:34:15.400 --> 00:34:15.800
kitchen.
厨房的那一幕。

832
00:34:16.100 --> 00:34:19.500
John is snapping his fingers like he's from West Side Story.
约翰打着响指，就像他是《西区故事》里的人一样。

833
00:34:19.500 --> 00:34:24.600
And we got tons of questions about these finger snaps, which I think is why I felt compelled
我们收到了很多关于这些响指的问题，我想这就是我为什么觉得有必要

834
00:34:24.600 --> 00:34:25.660
to write down the time code.
记下时间码的原因。

835
00:34:25.940 --> 00:34:28.900
The question was, was this scripted or improvised?
问题是，这是剧本写的还是即兴发挥的？

836
00:34:29.600 --> 00:34:34.860
I remember it as being improvised, and I remember being so tickled by it because I'm a huge movie
我记得是即兴发挥的，而且我当时觉得特别逗，因为我是个超级音乐剧迷，我问了李·艾森伯格，他也觉得是即兴的。

837
00:34:34.860 --> 00:34:39.260
musical fan, and I asked Lee Eisenberg, and he thinks it was also improvised.
他不记得写过那一幕。

838
00:34:39.380 --> 00:34:40.680
He does not remember writing that.
我不记得写过那一幕。

839
00:34:40.780 --> 00:34:46.160
I think it was improvised because it's just like John kind of playing around because earlier in the
我觉得是即兴的，因为那就像是约翰在玩闹，因为在节目

840
00:34:46.160 --> 00:34:48.480
show, he had mentioned, oh, like a jet.
早些时候，他提到了，哦，就像喷气机帮一样。

841
00:34:48.680 --> 00:34:51.040
And Michael, I think, thinks he's a jet.
我想迈克尔以为他真的是喷气机帮的人。

842
00:34:51.200 --> 00:34:52.660
He's like, oh, you're a jet.
他说，哦，你是喷气机帮的。

843
00:34:52.780 --> 00:34:54.540
That was the name of your actual gang.
那是你们真正的帮派名字。

844
00:34:54.700 --> 00:34:54.860
Yeah.
没错。

845
00:34:54.960 --> 00:34:57.120
So I think John is just playing off of that reference.
所以我认为约翰只是在顺着那个梗玩。

846
00:34:57.400 --> 00:34:58.200
It was so fun.
太有趣了。

847
00:34:58.200 --> 00:35:04.540
So then they go into the kitchen, and I have to say, this scene in the kitchen between Michael
然后他们走进厨房，我必须说，迈克尔和德怀特在厨房里

848
00:35:04.540 --> 00:35:11.040
and Dwight when they face off might be one of my favorite scenes from the entire second season
对峙的那一幕，可能是我在《办公室》第二季中

849
00:35:11.040 --> 00:35:11.620
of The Office.
最喜欢的场景之一。

850
00:35:12.060 --> 00:35:15.880
In the kitchen, John and I almost started laughing about a million times.
在厨房里，我和约翰差点笑场了上百万次。

851
00:35:16.080 --> 00:35:21.640
And if you notice, if you look at Mindy, she is constantly turning her back to the scene
如果你注意看明迪，你会发现她一直背对着现场，

852
00:35:21.640 --> 00:35:23.160
and looking into the annex.
往隔间那边看。

853
00:35:23.540 --> 00:35:25.720
I could see you and John almost break.
我能看出你和约翰差点就笑场了。

854
00:35:25.720 --> 00:35:29.780
When I watched this, knowing you guys, I was like, oh, they were about to lose it.
我看到这儿的时候，因为了解你们，我就想，噢，他们快要憋不住了。

855
00:35:29.960 --> 00:35:35.020
But seriously, watch Mindy through this because she cannot face the scene.
但说真的，这段戏一定要盯着明迪看，因为她根本不敢面对现场。

856
00:35:35.140 --> 00:35:35.680
It's amazing.
太绝了。

857
00:35:36.180 --> 00:35:42.820
Well, when Rain grabs her and is like, all right, now from behind, she's like, wait, what?
雷恩抓住她，说好了，现在从后面来，她当时肯定在想，等等，什么？

858
00:35:43.520 --> 00:35:43.960
Amazing.
太棒了。

859
00:35:44.100 --> 00:35:45.300
I don't know how she got through that.
我不知道她是怎么忍住没笑场的。

860
00:35:45.440 --> 00:35:47.440
And there's all these great things in this.
这里面有很多精彩的细节。

861
00:35:47.540 --> 00:35:51.240
This is the misuse of common phrases like catch 22.
比如对常用短语的误用，像“第22条军规”。

862
00:35:51.880 --> 00:35:52.780
Tit for tit.
“以牙还牙”（Tit for tit）。

863
00:35:52.980 --> 00:35:53.860
That's your favorite.
那是你的最爱。

864
00:35:53.860 --> 00:35:56.380
My favorite, this is the second time he has said it.
我的最爱，这已经是他第二次这么说了。

865
00:35:56.480 --> 00:35:57.260
Tit for tit.
“以牙还牙”。

866
00:35:57.960 --> 00:36:01.500
Also, two hits, me punching you and you hitting the floor.
还有，“两下重击”，我揍你一下，你倒地一下。

867
00:36:02.240 --> 00:36:03.320
It was so good.
太精彩了。

868
00:36:03.760 --> 00:36:05.260
It was just so good.
真的太精彩了。

869
00:36:05.460 --> 00:36:09.680
This leads me into my second time code, Angela.
这让我想到了我的第二个时间点，安吉拉。

870
00:36:09.880 --> 00:36:10.180
Okay.
好的。

871
00:36:10.980 --> 00:36:12.740
13 minutes, 27 seconds.
13分27秒。

872
00:36:13.220 --> 00:36:15.040
Well, I have one at 1325.
我这儿有个13分25秒的。

873
00:36:15.420 --> 00:36:16.260
All right, what's yours?
好吧，你的是什么？

874
00:36:16.500 --> 00:36:16.840
Let's see.
我看看。

875
00:36:16.840 --> 00:36:22.840
Well, this is at 1325, you see who actually goes to the dojo because you see everyone pile into the elevator.
在13分25秒，你可以看到到底是谁去了道场，因为大家全都挤进了电梯。

876
00:36:23.040 --> 00:36:27.520
And it is Phyllis, Pam, Meredith, Oscar, Creed, Kevin, Jim, Michael, and Dwight.
有菲利斯、帕姆、梅雷迪斯、奥斯卡、克里德、凯文、吉姆、迈克尔和德怀特。

877
00:36:27.660 --> 00:36:29.980
And who does not go to the dojo?
那谁没去道场呢？

878
00:36:30.720 --> 00:36:33.160
Angela, Stanley, Toby, Kelly, and Ryan.
安吉拉、斯坦利、托比、凯利和瑞安。

879
00:36:33.480 --> 00:36:34.420
Is that true?
真的吗？

880
00:36:34.420 --> 00:36:38.500
So you did not go to – did you not film that day when we went?
所以你没去——我们去拍的那天你没去吗？

881
00:36:38.500 --> 00:36:40.260
I had the day off.
那天我休假。

882
00:36:40.380 --> 00:36:41.620
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

883
00:36:41.760 --> 00:36:42.160
Yeah.
是啊。

884
00:36:42.160 --> 00:36:43.460
It was decadent.
那真是太奢侈了。

885
00:36:43.800 --> 00:36:44.840
It was decadent.
太奢侈了。

886
00:36:44.960 --> 00:36:45.100
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

887
00:36:45.260 --> 00:36:49.300
So when I talk about being at the dojo, you're going to hear what you missed out on.
所以当我谈到在道场的事时，你会听到你错过了什么。

888
00:36:49.380 --> 00:36:50.540
Yeah, I have no idea.
是啊，我完全不知道。

889
00:36:50.540 --> 00:36:55.660
Yeah, and, you know, the thinking was that Angela and Stanley would not participate in this.
是啊，你知道，当时的考虑是安吉拉和斯坦利不会参加这种活动。

890
00:36:55.780 --> 00:37:00.320
This is like shenanigans, and they are literally there to do work and clock in and clock out.
这简直是胡闹，他们来这儿纯粹是为了工作，准时打卡上下班。

891
00:37:00.440 --> 00:37:00.720
Yes.
没错。

892
00:37:00.900 --> 00:37:05.320
And so Angela and Stanley are really two of the big bah humbugs of the office.
所以安吉拉和斯坦利确实是办公室里两个大“扫兴鬼”。

893
00:37:05.660 --> 00:37:10.580
Toby and Kelly wouldn't go, or Ryan, because, as you know and I know, they were writers,
托比和凯利不会去，瑞安也不会，因为正如你我所知，他们是编剧，

894
00:37:10.580 --> 00:37:14.880
and they needed to be in the writer's room, and this was an opportunity for them to get some work done.
他们需要待在编剧室里，这正好是他们赶进度的好机会。

895
00:37:15.080 --> 00:37:16.480
Yes, it's so true.
没错，太对了。

896
00:37:16.880 --> 00:37:21.180
Well, when we all pile in the elevator, I don't know why I'm so tickled by it,
当我们全都挤进电梯时，我不知道为什么觉得特别好笑，

897
00:37:21.260 --> 00:37:26.820
but at 13 minutes and 27 seconds, just watch Kevin's face as the elevator doors close.
但在13分27秒，看看电梯门关上时凯文的表情。

898
00:37:27.160 --> 00:37:27.560
Okay.
好的。

899
00:37:27.700 --> 00:37:28.960
It just makes me laugh.
那真的让我笑个不停。

900
00:37:29.080 --> 00:37:29.420
All right.
好吧。

901
00:37:29.500 --> 00:37:31.600
He's got this little mischievous look on his face.
他脸上带着那种调皮的小表情。

902
00:37:31.600 --> 00:37:34.040
Like, he's very excited to see what's going to happen.
就好像他很兴奋，想看看接下来会发生什么。

903
00:37:34.240 --> 00:37:36.720
Totally like a little kid who got to leave school.
完全就像个刚放学的小孩。

904
00:37:36.940 --> 00:37:37.900
Oh, that's so cute.
噢，太可爱了。

905
00:37:37.920 --> 00:37:38.520
I love it.
我喜欢。

906
00:37:38.660 --> 00:37:38.880
All right.
好吧。

907
00:37:38.980 --> 00:37:41.440
Well, Angela, I'm going to tell you some stuff.
安吉拉，我要跟你说些事。

908
00:37:42.120 --> 00:37:46.960
The day that we shot at the dojo, it was really hot.
我们在道场拍摄的那天，天气特别热。

909
00:37:47.140 --> 00:37:49.340
I was going to say, were you guys all hot and sweaty?
我正想问呢，你们当时是不是都热得大汗淋漓？

910
00:37:49.580 --> 00:37:50.000
Yes.
是啊。

911
00:37:50.140 --> 00:37:53.240
And the air conditioning in our trailers wasn't working.
而且我们拖车里的空调坏了。

912
00:37:53.480 --> 00:37:53.800
Oh.
噢。

913
00:37:54.060 --> 00:37:56.760
So remember on the dundies when they had ants?
还记得拍“邓迪奖”那集时，现场有蚂蚁吗？

914
00:37:56.980 --> 00:38:01.900
This time, they had no air conditioning, and they're metal.
这次是没空调，而且拖车是金属做的。

915
00:38:02.380 --> 00:38:05.500
So it was kind of like changing your clothes in a sauna,
所以换衣服简直就像在桑拿房里一样，

916
00:38:05.500 --> 00:38:10.220
and we were just super sweaty, all of us, and gross.
我们所有人都汗流浃背，难受极了。

917
00:38:10.500 --> 00:38:12.520
And I had to wear a sweater.
而且我还得穿件毛衣。

918
00:38:12.740 --> 00:38:12.940
Yeah.
是啊。

919
00:38:13.100 --> 00:38:16.240
Because we had established my beige sweater earlier in the office.
因为我们之前在办公室里已经设定好我穿那件米色毛衣了。

920
00:38:16.460 --> 00:38:21.780
And I remember thinking, oh, my God, I am so sweaty and stinky,
我记得当时心想，天哪，我身上又热又臭，

921
00:38:21.780 --> 00:38:24.620
and John has to pick me up.
而约翰还得抱我。

922
00:38:25.020 --> 00:38:29.400
This is a thing that I think people don't think about.
这是我觉得大家平时不会去想的一点。

923
00:38:29.920 --> 00:38:33.600
You know, anytime I would have a scene where I would have to whisper at someone
你知道，每当我有需要跟人耳语的戏份，

924
00:38:33.600 --> 00:38:37.280
or you'd have to kiss, I would brush my teeth like three times
或者需要接吻的时候，我都会刷三次牙，

925
00:38:37.280 --> 00:38:39.520
and chew gum and eat a mint before.
还要嚼口香糖，吃颗薄荷糖。

926
00:38:39.960 --> 00:38:42.440
And anytime when you have to be close to someone,
每当需要跟人靠得很近时，

927
00:38:42.720 --> 00:38:46.640
I would be very aware of my potential body odor.
我都会非常在意自己身上有没有异味。

928
00:38:47.580 --> 00:38:50.880
At least our show wasn't a show with a bunch of close talkers.
好在我们剧里没有那种喜欢贴脸说话的角色。

929
00:38:50.960 --> 00:38:53.440
Because you watch an episode of The Sopranos.
因为你看《黑道家族》的时候，

930
00:38:53.440 --> 00:38:54.780
They get in each other's faces.
他们说话时脸都贴在一起。

931
00:38:54.780 --> 00:38:55.840
They're like, listen here.
他们会说，你给我听着。

932
00:38:56.060 --> 00:38:57.920
And they're right up to each other's face.
脸都快贴到对方脸上了。

933
00:38:58.000 --> 00:38:59.300
At least we didn't have that.
至少我们没那种情况。

934
00:38:59.460 --> 00:39:00.000
That's true.
确实。

935
00:39:00.060 --> 00:39:03.220
But when I watched those scenes, because we're actors and we know,
但当我看到那些戏份时，因为我们是演员，我们懂，

936
