1091
00:45:36.340 --> 00:45:39.560
All right, so after this humiliating defeat,
好了，在这场丢脸的失败之后，

1092
00:45:39.560 --> 00:45:50.220
we go back to the office and we see a scene from Michael's office that goes down into the parking lot and he tries to call Ryan on his cell phone.
我们回到办公室，看到迈克尔办公室的一个场景，镜头移向停车场，他试图用手机给瑞安打电话。

1093
00:45:50.780 --> 00:45:54.240
That was a different office than the usual Michael's office.
那间办公室和通常迈克尔的办公室不一样。

1094
00:45:54.460 --> 00:45:56.880
You totally, like, it's completely different.
你完全能看出来，它完全不同。

1095
00:45:57.180 --> 00:45:57.440
Yes.
是的。

1096
00:45:57.560 --> 00:45:59.480
So we had two Michael's offices.
所以我们有两个迈克尔的办公室。

1097
00:45:59.780 --> 00:46:12.900
We had one Michael's office that was on our set and it had just like a scrim backdrop behind the window that was kind of blurry and it was just like an old-fashioned fake out the window kind of thing.
一个是我们在片场搭建的迈克尔办公室，窗户后面只是一个模糊的幕布背景，就像那种老式的假窗户。

1098
00:46:12.900 --> 00:46:21.440
But whenever we had to shoot a scene where Michael was actually looking out of his window into the parking lot, we would move over to the writer's offices.
但每当我们需要拍摄迈克尔从窗户往停车场看的场景时，我们就会搬到编剧办公室去拍。

1099
00:46:21.720 --> 00:46:24.400
And they literally would shoot in a writer's office.
他们真的是在编剧的办公室里拍摄的。

1100
00:46:24.620 --> 00:46:24.900
Yes.
是的。

1101
00:46:25.040 --> 00:46:30.000
And I was trying to remember, was it Mike Schur's office or Paul Lieberstein's office?
我当时在努力回想，那是迈克·舒尔的办公室还是保罗·利伯斯坦的办公室？

1102
00:46:30.600 --> 00:46:34.920
One of the two of them worked in Michael's office.
他们俩其中一人在迈克的办公室里办公。

1103
00:46:35.120 --> 00:46:35.200
Right.
没错。

1104
00:46:35.200 --> 00:46:37.620
And it was loosely decorated as Michael's office.
而且那间办公室被简单布置成了迈克的办公室。

1105
00:46:37.620 --> 00:46:43.440
And then when it was time to shoot, they would get kicked out of their office and set dressing would come in and zhuzh it up.
等到要拍摄的时候，他们就得被赶出办公室，然后布景师会进来进行一番装饰。

1106
00:46:43.980 --> 00:46:47.740
And then they would have to use that to shoot and they couldn't write in their office that day.
之后他们就得在那儿拍戏，那天他们就没法在自己的办公室里写剧本了。

1107
00:46:47.840 --> 00:46:50.400
But the walls are like kind of a green color.
但墙壁颜色有点偏绿。

1108
00:46:50.500 --> 00:46:51.980
Yes, that was always true.
是的，这一点一直没变。

1109
00:46:52.640 --> 00:46:53.500
That don't match.
那颜色对不上。

1110
00:46:53.500 --> 00:46:56.040
Like, I was like, guys, the walls are not the same.
我就想，伙计们，墙的颜色不一样啊。

1111
00:46:56.340 --> 00:47:00.340
Well, it's funny, too, because all the other writers could decorate their offices.
嗯，这很有趣，因为其他编剧都可以装饰自己的办公室。

1112
00:47:00.640 --> 00:47:02.180
Oh, Mindy's office was so decorated.
噢，敏迪的办公室装饰得可漂亮了。

1113
00:47:02.400 --> 00:47:02.760
Oh, for sure.
那肯定的。

1114
00:47:02.860 --> 00:47:03.260
Of course.
当然了。

1115
00:47:03.380 --> 00:47:03.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1116
00:47:03.740 --> 00:47:04.060
Of course.
当然。

1117
00:47:04.240 --> 00:47:07.240
But you could have like personal photos up and posters on the wall.
但你可以放些个人照片，墙上也能贴海报。

1118
00:47:07.620 --> 00:47:09.180
But they couldn't do it.
可他们却不能那样做。

1119
00:47:09.300 --> 00:47:10.260
I feel like it was Paul's.
我觉得那是保罗的办公室。

1120
00:47:10.280 --> 00:47:11.520
I think it was Paul's as well.
我也觉得是保罗的。

1121
00:47:11.640 --> 00:47:11.960
Because I remember.
因为我记得。

1122
00:47:11.960 --> 00:47:12.620
That's my memory.
我是这么记得的。

1123
00:47:12.820 --> 00:47:16.120
If it wasn't Paul's, then Paul just really didn't make a lot of effort to decorate.
如果那不是保罗的办公室，那保罗在装饰上确实没花什么心思。

1124
00:47:16.340 --> 00:47:17.040
One of the two.
二选一吧。

1125
00:47:17.220 --> 00:47:18.680
I remember his office being pretty bare.
我记得他的办公室挺空荡的。

1126
00:47:19.300 --> 00:47:24.140
So next up, Michael tells the rest of us to sign the forMs.
接下来，迈克让我们其他人去签那些表格。

1127
00:47:24.620 --> 00:47:25.580
He's given up.
他放弃了。

1128
00:47:25.680 --> 00:47:26.060
For sure.
肯定的。

1129
00:47:26.280 --> 00:47:30.800
At the end of the show, the people who actually signed the reports are Toby, Stanley, Angela, and Pam.
在剧集结尾，真正签了报告的人是托比、斯坦利、安吉拉和帕姆。

1130
00:47:30.800 --> 00:47:33.860
And we were all grouped together at the reception desk.
我们当时都聚在前台那边。

1131
00:47:33.900 --> 00:47:38.380
And I loved shooting that scene because everyone else had gone home for the day.
我很喜欢拍那场戏，因为其他人都已经下班回家了。

1132
00:47:38.580 --> 00:47:39.680
Except for Dwight.
除了德怀特。

1133
00:47:39.860 --> 00:47:40.420
That's right.
没错。

1134
00:47:40.600 --> 00:47:41.660
Who was at his desk.
他当时坐在自己的办公桌前。

1135
00:47:41.960 --> 00:47:43.780
But most of the office was gone.
但办公室里大部分人都走了。

1136
00:47:44.000 --> 00:47:48.760
And that group of us, we were very rarely in little scenes together.
我们那一小群人很少有机会一起拍戏。

1137
00:47:49.000 --> 00:47:49.900
Just us.
就我们几个。

1138
00:47:50.020 --> 00:47:52.060
And I have very fond memories of shooting that.
我对拍摄那场戏留下了非常美好的回忆。

1139
00:47:52.200 --> 00:47:52.620
Me, too.
我也是。

1140
00:47:52.780 --> 00:47:53.140
Me, too.
我也是。

1141
00:47:53.260 --> 00:47:54.380
That was really, really fun.
那真的非常非常有意思。

1142
00:47:54.380 --> 00:47:59.460
I have one thing that is a time code that was right before the end there.
我有一个时间码，就在结尾之前。

1143
00:47:59.700 --> 00:48:03.940
At 17 minutes, 57 seconds, people are packing up for the day.
在17分57秒的时候，大家都在收拾东西准备下班。

1144
00:48:04.620 --> 00:48:06.800
Guess who's sitting across from Meredith?
猜猜谁坐在梅雷迪思对面？

1145
00:48:07.580 --> 00:48:08.140
Who?
谁？

1146
00:48:08.620 --> 00:48:09.180
Ryan.
瑞安。

1147
00:48:09.560 --> 00:48:10.820
Yeah, that was his desk.
对，那是他的办公桌。

1148
00:48:11.000 --> 00:48:12.040
But where was Creed?
但克里德在哪儿？

1149
00:48:12.720 --> 00:48:14.900
Creed didn't really have a desk yet.
克里德当时还没真正拥有自己的办公桌。

1150
00:48:15.060 --> 00:48:16.620
I don't know.
我不知道。

1151
00:48:16.860 --> 00:48:19.080
When does Creed take over Ryan's desk?
克里德是什么时候接手瑞安办公桌的？

1152
00:48:19.100 --> 00:48:21.000
And when does Ryan move back to the annex?
瑞安又是什么时候搬回附楼的？

1153
00:48:22.160 --> 00:48:23.340
These are good questions.
这些都是好问题。

1154
00:48:23.580 --> 00:48:23.880
I know.
我知道。

1155
00:48:23.880 --> 00:48:24.700
Did Ryan?
瑞安搬过吗？

1156
00:48:24.860 --> 00:48:29.560
Well, eventually, remember, we turned that closet in the hallway into Ryan's office, I feel like.
嗯，最终搬了，记得吗，我感觉我们把走廊里的那个储物间改成了瑞安的办公室。

1157
00:48:29.560 --> 00:48:30.440
Yeah, for a little bit.
对，有一阵子是那样。

1158
00:48:30.600 --> 00:48:32.700
That desk was kind of the catch-all, right?
那张桌子就像是个杂物堆，对吧？

1159
00:48:32.800 --> 00:48:34.380
I feel like I've seen Devin there.
我感觉我见过德文在那儿坐过。

1160
00:48:34.560 --> 00:48:35.300
I've seen Ryan there.
我见过瑞安在那儿坐过。

1161
00:48:35.380 --> 00:48:36.180
I've seen Creed there.
我见过克里德在那儿坐过。

1162
00:48:36.320 --> 00:48:38.720
When does it become Creed's desk?
那它是什么时候变成克里德的办公桌的？

1163
00:48:39.000 --> 00:48:43.920
Also, in this episode, at the end, when people are filing out, we see an appearance of Luann.
另外，在这一集的结尾，当大家鱼贯而出时，我们看到了卢安出镜。

1164
00:48:44.260 --> 00:48:45.420
Oh, there's Luann.
噢，那是卢安。

1165
00:48:45.700 --> 00:48:46.100
Luann.
卢安。

1166
00:48:46.240 --> 00:48:48.980
Luann was one of our stand-in slash extras.
卢安是我们的一位替身兼临时演员。

1167
00:48:48.980 --> 00:48:50.520
Who would normally sit in the annex.
她通常坐在附楼里。

1168
00:48:50.720 --> 00:48:52.120
And people always say, who is that?
大家总会问，那是谁？

1169
00:48:52.220 --> 00:48:53.340
So Luann walks by.
所以卢安走过去了。

1170
00:48:53.340 --> 00:48:54.040
That's right.
没错。

1171
00:48:54.240 --> 00:49:01.880
I feel like the two things I want to tell you guys we're going to be dedicated to tracking in this rewatch is Mindy's hair and when does Creed get his desk.
我觉得有两件事我想告诉你们，我们会在这次重温中专门追踪，一个是明迪的发型，另一个是克里德什么时候得到他的办公桌。

1172
00:49:02.400 --> 00:49:02.880
Okay?
好吗？

1173
00:49:03.180 --> 00:49:03.980
So just know that.
所以记住了。

1174
00:49:04.240 --> 00:49:05.860
Someone out there probably already knows.
外面可能已经有人知道了。

1175
00:49:05.860 --> 00:49:09.320
They're going to write in and say, you guys, Creed sits there in episode.
他们会写信来说，嘿你们，克里德在第几集坐在那儿。

1176
00:49:09.540 --> 00:49:10.160
Tell us.
告诉我们吧。

1177
00:49:10.260 --> 00:49:10.740
Tell us.
告诉我们吧。

1178
00:49:10.740 --> 00:49:11.840
Solve this mystery.
解开这个谜团。

1179
00:49:12.340 --> 00:49:12.540
Okay.
好的。

1180
00:49:13.760 --> 00:49:22.800
Michael takes Dwight into the conference room here at the end, and he says he's been testing him all day, and he promotes Dwight to assistant regional manager.
迈克尔在结尾把德怀特叫进会议室，说他整天都在考验他，然后他提拔德怀特为助理区域经理。

1181
00:49:23.140 --> 00:49:23.600
Right.
没错。

1182
00:49:23.600 --> 00:49:28.420
He gets no announcement, no raise, and no new office, but Dwight is so happy.
他没有得到任何公告、加薪，也没有新办公室，但德怀特却非常高兴。

1183
00:49:28.460 --> 00:49:29.180
He's so happy.
他太高兴了。

1184
00:49:29.180 --> 00:49:32.280
He whites out to the on all of his business cards.
他把他所有名片上的“助理”字样都用涂改液涂掉了。

1185
00:49:34.000 --> 00:49:36.800
It's so pure and sweet.
真是纯真又可爱。

1186
00:49:37.080 --> 00:49:37.560
I know.
我知道。

1187
00:49:37.560 --> 00:49:38.440
It's so sweet.
太可爱了。

1188
00:49:38.440 --> 00:49:41.440
Although Michael's like, it's not really a real thing, but it doesn't really matter.
虽然迈克尔说，这其实不是个真正的职位，但这并不重要。

1189
00:49:41.620 --> 00:49:43.320
Dwight isn't hearing that part.
德怀特根本没听进去那部分。

1190
00:49:43.620 --> 00:49:46.580
He doesn't hear any words except assistant regional manager.
除了“助理区域经理”，他什么话都听不进去。

1191
00:49:46.580 --> 00:49:53.020
And then this leads us to the famous Michael talking headline, Would I Rather Be Feared or Loved?
然后这就引出了迈克尔那段著名的独白：“我更希望被畏惧还是被爱戴？”

1192
00:49:53.240 --> 00:49:53.720
Easy.
很简单。

1193
00:49:54.100 --> 00:49:54.580
Both.
两者都要。

1194
00:49:54.840 --> 00:49:57.660
I want people to be afraid of how much they love me.
我希望人们因为太爱我而感到畏惧。

1195
00:49:57.940 --> 00:50:00.200
I have seen that stitched on pillows.
我见过这句话被绣在枕头上。

1196
00:50:00.480 --> 00:50:02.020
I have seen that on shirts.
我见过这句话印在衬衫上。

1197
00:50:02.640 --> 00:50:05.080
I want people to be afraid of how much they love me.
我希望人们因为太爱我而感到畏惧。

1198
00:50:05.320 --> 00:50:06.480
Good writers.
好编剧。

1199
00:50:07.060 --> 00:50:08.080
Such good writing.
写得真好。

1200
00:50:08.400 --> 00:50:10.580
And that was the fight.
这就是那场争吵。

1201
00:50:10.780 --> 00:50:11.640
That was the fight.
那就是那场争执。

1202
00:50:11.640 --> 00:50:16.440
So next week, we will be back with the client.
所以下周，我们将回到“客户”那一集。

1203
00:50:16.780 --> 00:50:17.600
The client.
“客户”。

1204
00:50:17.660 --> 00:50:21.340
This is maybe my favorite season two episode.
这可能是我最喜欢的第二季剧集。

1205
00:50:21.520 --> 00:50:23.120
Although there's also the injury.
虽然还有关于受伤的情节。

1206
00:50:23.360 --> 00:50:24.080
I love the injury.
我喜欢受伤的情节。

1207
00:50:24.180 --> 00:50:25.780
You love the injury, Jenna.
你喜欢受伤的情节，珍娜。

1208
00:50:25.900 --> 00:50:25.980
I know.
我知道。

1209
00:50:25.980 --> 00:50:30.720
You wore a shirt that you've bought online of the injury.
你穿过一件在网上买的关于受伤情节的衬衫。

1210
00:50:30.720 --> 00:50:34.020
I bought a shirt from Etsy of a grilled foot for a long time.
我曾很长一段时间都穿着一件从Etsy上买的印有烤焦的脚的衬衫。

1211
00:50:34.020 --> 00:50:34.980
Yeah, that you would wear.
是啊，你确实会穿。

1212
00:50:35.080 --> 00:50:35.380
For a long time.
穿了很久。

1213
00:50:35.740 --> 00:50:37.060
You would wear it a lot.
你经常穿它。

1214
00:50:37.220 --> 00:50:38.480
It was like one of your favorite shirts.
它就像你最喜欢的衬衫之一。

1215
00:50:38.520 --> 00:50:39.600
Geez, did it bother you?
天哪，那让你感到困扰了吗？

1216
00:50:39.900 --> 00:50:40.500
It didn't.
并没有。

1217
00:50:40.500 --> 00:50:41.680
Did I wear it too often?
我穿得太频繁了吗？

1218
00:50:41.840 --> 00:50:42.480
No, it didn't.
没有，并没有。

1219
00:50:42.560 --> 00:50:43.600
But it just made me laugh.
但它只是让我觉得好笑。

1220
00:50:43.780 --> 00:50:47.820
There was a day that you showed up in your shirt with the grilled foot.
有一天你穿着那件印有烤焦的脚的衬衫出现了。

1221
00:50:48.040 --> 00:50:54.300
And I had a shirt that was like an inside joke on our show of Creed as an action figure in Hong Kong.
而我当时穿了一件关于我们剧集内部梗的衬衫，上面是克里德作为香港动作人偶的图案。

1222
00:50:54.640 --> 00:50:54.980
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1223
00:50:55.720 --> 00:50:58.400
Did we realize we were maybe too big of fans?
我们有没有意识到我们可能太迷恋这部剧了？

1224
00:50:58.660 --> 00:51:00.640
We were like, what are we doing?
我们当时想，我们在干什么？

1225
00:51:00.680 --> 00:51:02.440
We're just walking around in shirts from our show.
我们竟然穿着自己剧集的周边衬衫到处走。

1226
00:51:02.600 --> 00:51:06.580
So next week, we will be talking about not the injury, but the client.
所以下周，我们要讨论的不是“受伤”，而是“客户”。

1227
00:51:06.860 --> 00:51:07.620
We'll see you then.
到时见。

1228
00:51:07.720 --> 00:51:08.140
See you then.
到时见。

